    {
      "id": "6c625a4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7.Important High-Yield Points"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2o2jywi",
      "content": "1. Fat-soluble vitamins (A, D, E, K) are stored in liver and adipose tissue."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pg6wxko",
      "content": "2. Water-soluble vitamins (B-complex, C) are generally not stored and excess is excreted in urine."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1c0y4zl",
      "content": "3. Vitamin B12 absorption requires intrinsic factor secreted by stomach."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Property",
        "Fat-Soluble Vitamins",
        "Water-Soluble Vitamins"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Vitamins Included",
          "Vitamin A, D, E, and K",
          "Vitamin B-complex and Vitamin C"
        ],
        [
          "Storage Location",
          "Stored in liver and adipose tissues",
          "Not stored in body; excreted in urine"
        ],
        [
          "Excretion & Toxicity",
          "Excreted slowly; excess can cause Hypervitaminosis",
          "Excreted easily; low risk of toxicity"
        ],
        [
          "Absorption",
          "Requires dietary fat and bile salts for absorption",
          "Absorbed directly into the bloodstream with water"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "zdtefp0"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fdwv177",
      "content": "4. Vitamin K is essential for synthesis of prothrombin in blood clotting."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "86mbbsr",
      "content": "5. Pellagra (Niacin deficiency) is characterized by 3 D's – Dermatitis, Diarrhea, Dementia."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pwkm5ku",
      "content": "6. Rickets occurs in children; Osteomalacia occurs in adults (Vitamin D deficiency)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "70dv24e",
      "content": "7. Hypervitaminosis mainly occurs with fat-soluble vitamins."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pnihkpz",
      "content": "8. Vitamin C enhances iron absorption in intestine."
    },
